<CapyPlopInfo title="Support" description="Help with Capy Plop controls, local progress, Hot Springs Pass purchases, restores and optional promotions.">
  <p>Capy Plop is a native game for iPhone and iPad running iOS or iPadOS 17 or later, provided by Randy Torres under the RandyVentures name.</p>
  <p>For help, email <a href="mailto:randyventures06@gmail.com?subject=Capy%20Plop%20support">randyventures06@gmail.com</a>. Include your device, system version, Capy Plop version/build from Settings, and what happened. A screenshot can help. Please leave out passwords, payment-card details and private information unrelated to the problem. You can use TestFlight's feedback tools when testing a beta.</p>
  <h2>How to hop</h2>
  <p>Press and hold on the springs or the hop button to charge, then release to jump. Aim for the middle of the next pool. Settings offers tap-to-charge, tap-to-jump controls. Trail 1 introduces the landing guide. You can pause at any time; wait on the current safe spring when a water hazard warns before bursting.</p>
  <h2>What is on the capybara's head?</h2>
  <p>It is an outfit, starting with a little orange. The accessories stay attached and are cosmetic: they do not add weight, change jump distance, provide extra lives or alter scoring. Earn the leaf at 25 lifetime plops. Towel, Blossom, Duck and Crown are included with the optional Hot Springs Pass.</p>
  <h2>Trails, stars and practice</h2>
  <p>The thirty trails unlock in order. The first ten Cedar trails are included; the remaining twenty require the Pass as well as completing the preceding trail. Replay a trail to improve its stars. Daily and weekly challenges also require the Pass and use UTC dates: daily resets at midnight UTC; weekly resets on Monday at midnight UTC. Practice offers wider pools and a landing guide without raising your endless best score.</p>
  <h2>Optional promotions and continues</h2>
  <p>After at least one successful hop, a miss can offer one continue. Choose Save my run and watch the stated time in the native ad view, then choose Continue run. Only visible foreground viewing counts; covering the ad with the report sheet or leaving the app pauses its timer. Skip or dismissal earns no reward. You do not need to tap an App Store link, download, rate or buy anything. A new attempt is always available without a lives or energy meter.</p>
  <p>Pass owners receive that continue without watching an ad. Continued runs are assisted: they do not set clean records or dated medals, and a campaign clear earns one star without reducing stars already earned. The once-per-run limit applies to everyone.</p>
  <p>Use About this ad to inspect the information used for selection, report an inappropriate creative, or hide it locally. Report opens your chosen email/share interface; nothing is sent until you send it. The in-app reporting address can differ from the general support address above. You may also email general support with the advertised app name and a screenshot.</p>
  <h2>Hot Springs Pass and restores</h2>
  <p>The Pass is a one-time, non-consumable in-app purchase, not a subscription. It adds twenty trails, Blossom and Moonlight worlds, daily and weekly challenges, practice, four outfits and an ad-free continue. Owning it does not skip earlier trails. Apple's purchase sheet shows the localized price before you confirm. Apple handles payment; we do not receive your card details.</p>
  <p>To recover the Pass, sign in to the Apple Account used to buy it and choose Restore Purchases in the shop or Settings while online. The Pass can be restored on your compatible devices using that account. Family Sharing is not enabled. Local scores and stars do not transfer with a restored purchase. Refund requests go through <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">Apple's Report a Problem service</a>; a refund or revoked purchase can remove Pass access.</p>
  <p>If the shop cannot load, check your connection, Apple Account and device purchase restrictions, then reload the shop. Pending Ask to Buy requests must be approved before access unlocks. For purchase help, you may include the optional Purchase support ID shown in Settings; it lets us locate the associated RevenueCat purchase record. Do not send your Apple password or full receipt unless needed and requested.</p>
  <p>Debug playtest builds may say “Test unlock · no charge” and use RevenueCat Test Store. TestFlight uses Apple's sandbox and does not charge for sandbox purchases. Test unlocks are not paid App Store purchases and may not carry into a production installation.</p>
  <h2>Keep your progress</h2>
  <p>Best scores, lifetime plops, trail stars, medals, outfit choices and settings are saved locally after successful hops and changes. They do not sync between devices. Update the existing app in place; do not delete it to update. Deleting the app or choosing Reset local progress can remove that device's progress. A device backup may contain saves, but the app cannot guarantee recovery. Resetting progress does not remove a valid purchased Pass.</p>
  <p>If a save-recovery notice appears, stop resetting or reinstalling and contact support with the exact message. We cannot remotely read or restore your local gameplay save.</p>
  <h2>Offline play and device features</h2>
  <p>Gameplay and local progress work without a network connection. Purchase/restore and catalog updates require connectivity. Previously verified Pass access uses Apple's local transaction cache; refunds or account changes may require another online check. Promotions have a bundled/cached fallback. Turn sound and haptics on or off in Settings; Reduce Motion follows the system setting. Haptics depend on device hardware.</p>
</CapyPlopInfo>
